Observed metadata:

```txt
docId: patterns-for-building-ai-agents-1-3cdbfd2f64df
title: Patterns for Building AI Agents 1
file_type: pdf
document_type: book
storage_category: programming
page_count: 93
primary_concept_id: jc:docs:programming
source_host: dark-wizard
```

Why it matters for this project:

- It has sections on agent configuration and architecture.
- It has a context-engineering section that search surfaced for parallel subagents, sharing context, avoiding context failure modes, compressing context, and feeding errors into context.
- It has evaluation material that can inform verifier contracts.
- It has security material that can inform tool audit, prompt-injection boundaries, and access control.

Keep future capture source-backed and ref-heavy. Use chunk links as receipts, not as pasted corpus.

## Useful research captures for this repo

### 1. JoelClaw Docs API source adapter

Research target: turn JoelClaw docs search into a reusable context-pack/source-pack workflow.

Shape:

```txt
researchIntent
→ joelclawSearch
→ fetchDocMetadataAndToc
→ selectChunks
→ assembleSourcePack
→ verifyClaimsAgainstChunks
→ persistBrainResource
```

Events:

```txt
JOELCLAW_SEARCH_REQUESTED
DOC_HIT_SELECTED
TOC_FETCHED
CHUNK_SELECTED
SOURCE_PACK_ASSEMBLED
CLAIMS_VERIFIED
BRAIN_NOTE_PERSISTED
```

Pi mapping:

- Context capsule records query URLs, selected `docId`s, selected `chunkId`s, and source-pack refs.
- Worker lanes may fetch/search JoelClaw, but a verifier lane must check claims before Brain persistence.
- Artifacts should store query receipts and source-pack manifests, not full private/paid text dumps.
- Brain notes should link to JoelClaw API refs and summarize reusable decisions.

Why first: it turns the corpus into repeatable fuel for `research-claude-workflows` instead of one-off search spelunking.

