Capture questions:

- What is the minimum verification contract card?
- Which properties must every generated workflow machine satisfy?
- How do we test cancel/cleanup, retry idempotency, HITL resume, and bounded concurrency?
- How do verifier lanes distinguish accepted warnings from blocking failures?

Expected Brain output: `.brain/resources/workflow-verifier-evals-playbook.svx`.

Completed prototype receipt:

```txt
run: run-joelclaw-research-swarm-workflow-verifier-evals-96a02bd9
prototype: prototypes/joelclaw-research-swarm-spike/
public research output: https://pi-joelclaw-research-swarm-spike.joelhooks.workers.dev/research/joelclaw-research-swarm-workflow-verifier-evals
public observer: https://pi-joelclaw-research-swarm-spike.joelhooks.workers.dev/observer/joelclaw-research-swarm-workflow-verifier-evals
Artifacts repo: jcrs-run-joelclaw-research-swarm-workflow-verifier-evals-96a02bd9
research lanes: 6 real Pi internet-research agent lanes
model: openai-codex/gpt-5.5
max observed active lanes: 3
source refs: 62
verifier: verified
final state: captured
output refs: .brain/resources/workflow-verifier-evals-playbook.svx, capsule:inline-bibliography, capsule:inline-source-map
Brain page: .brain/resources/workflow-verifier-evals-playbook.svx
Brain URL: https://pi-notes-4188.localhost/notes/resources/workflow-verifier-evals-playbook
```

Implementation lessons:

- Bounded hot concurrency beat cold-start stampede; the clean run used 3 active Sandboxes across 6 total lanes.
- Queue messages need run-id guards because stale retry messages can outlive a capsule run.
- Real lane scripts need explicit env shape (`LANE_ID`, `LANE_JSON`) and should avoid ambiguous Node module syntax.
- The corrected research run materialized Pi auth, pinned a project-local `.pi/extensions/research-tools.ts`, exposed Brave/URL/JoelClaw research tools to Pi, and invoked `pi -e .pi/extensions/research-tools.ts --provider openai-codex --model gpt-5.5` inside each research Sandbox; lane receipts record `runtime: pi-agent-internet-research`.

